ATMS 523 - FINAL PROJECT

The Identification of Moisture Pathways Associated with Widespread Extreme Precipitation in the Great Lakes

This project investigates the role of large-scale moisture transport and moisture flux convergence (MFC) in driving widespread extreme precipitation events over the Great Lakes region. 
Using ERA5 reanalysis and Stage IV precipitation data, the study links moisture dynamics (Domain 2) to regional-scale extreme precipitation impacts (Domain 1).

Requirements:
xarray, numpy, pandas
metpy
scikit-learn
eofs
shap
matplotlib, cartopy
bokeh
